WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
A star is a tug of war.

2
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.110
Gravity pulls every layer inwards.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.770
Pressure from hot gas and
radiation pushes outwards.

4
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.140
Fusion in the core keeps it going.

5
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.000
Huge forces, zero resultant.

6
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.930
The star is stable.

7
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.420
But sooner or later, the
core's hydrogen runs out.

8
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.680
So why will the Sun end
as a small, fading ember,

9
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.260
while far heavier stars
blow themselves apart?

10
00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.190
In this mission, you'll
read the HR diagram:

11
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.780
luminosity up the side,
temperature falling to the right.

12
00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:36.640
Then you'll see that a star does not
simply slide along the main sequence as it

13
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.590
ages.

14
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.420
Your mission: explain why
the Sun's ending is so quiet,

15
00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.650
and heavier stars' so violent.
